item.text:
{
  "concepts": [
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "F16, Engagement baseline, is an operational profile. Its foundation-to-law table traces premises, consequences, owning rules, added choices and pillars; it distinguishes imported consequences from choices owned by this profile or the adopting Product.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":199,
          "quote":"This member is material family F16, Engagement baseline (operational\nprofile). The table below shows which of its rules follow from which\npremises, in the format of\n",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F3.%20Engagement%20applicability%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":197
        }
      ],
      "key":"engagement_baseline",
      "label":"Engagement baseline F16"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Imported families are F1 frames and context; F2 transitions, steps and configuration; F3 results and combination; F4 work state, resumption and reuse; F5 proportionality and cost; F6 claims, evidence, assessment and acceptance; F15 product lineage objects; and F13 work carriers, including independent-review boundaries and closure. Their consequences serve as premises without transferring ownership to this profile.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":219,
          "quote":"A row that\ncites an imported family uses that family's consequences as premises; the\nrules that state them keep their owners, and the choice column names them\nas imported, never as this profile's choices.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F3.%20Engagement%20applicability%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":216
        }
      ],
      "key":"imported_method_families",
      "label":"Imported method families"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The trace reports P0 as recovered; P1, P2, P3, P4a and P6 as independent; P4b as derived from P0 and P2 with the premise that step-produced facts are not re-acquirable; and P5 as derived from P0 and P6 with P0's open-world premise. Instance premises I1–I3 are adopted only with the executive configuration: bounded tasks under one outcome need separate construction and delivery attention; existing project authority holds every decision grant; actors have finite context and attention, are fallible, and constructors may be probabilistic.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":225,
          "quote":"Standing of the commitments\ncited ([FOUNDATIONS §3](FOUNDATIONS.md#3-commitments)): P0 recovered; P1,\nP2, P3, P4a and P6 independent; P4b derived from P0 and P2, with P0's\npremise that step-produced facts are not re-acquirable; P5 derived from P0\nand P6, with P0's open-world premise. Its instance premises hold where\nthe executive configuration is selected; they are adopted with it and do\nnot follow from the foundations (P1, P6):",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F3.%20Engagement%20applicability%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":219
        },
        {
          "end_line":234,
          "quote":"- I1: the work is a series of bounded tasks under one governed outcome,\n  and carrying out a bounded change and managing delivery across the tasks\n  need separate attention;\n- I2: existing project authority (Goals, Product, requirements, accepted\n  design, a work item, identity or release law) holds every decision grant\n  the configuration applies;\n- I3: the actors are fallible and have finite context and attention, and a\n  constructing actor may be probabilistic.\n",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F3.%20Engagement%20applicability%2FFoundation%20to%20law",
          "start_line":227
        }
      ],
      "key":"foundation_and_instance_premises",
      "label":"Foundation standing and instance premises"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "An engagement frame is a frame whose evaluation family concerns selecting, constructing, assessing or disposing governed work. Executive, Worker and Reviewer are this profile's engagement frames.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":342,
          "quote":"An engagement frame is a frame (REFERENCE_FRAME §1) whose evaluation family\nconcerns selecting, constructing, assessing or disposing governed work.\nExecutive, Worker and Reviewer are this profile's engagement frames (P1;\nrc.2 #engagement-frame).\n",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FEngagement%20frame",
          "start_line":339
        }
      ],
      "key":"engagement_frame",
      "label":"Engagement frame"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A specialist frame is an activated Product, requirement, design, identity, release, domain, implementation, test, operational, historical or capability frame needed by one engagement evaluation.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":348,
          "quote":"A specialist frame is an activated Product, requirement, design, identity,\nrelease, domain, implementation, test, operational, historical or\ncapability frame that one engagement evaluation needs.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FSpecialist%20frame",
          "start_line":346
        }
      ],
      "key":"specialist_frame",
      "label":"Specialist frame"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A generic specialist-frame family is a reusable evaluation archetype naming a recurring distinction. It selects no concrete carrier, component, actor, architecture, owner or implementation. Its labels resolve in urn:stdo:bounded-context:reference-frame-evaluation, owned by REFERENCE_FRAME under the selected basis; same-spelled concepts in other contexts are not thereby identical.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":360,
          "quote":"A generic specialist-frame family is a reusable evaluation-family archetype\nof this profile (§11). It names a recurring distinction that a project\neither instantiates where material, has capable authority establish as\nnon-material for the governed outcome, or keeps as an explicit coverage\nresidual (P2, P6; rc.2 #generic-specialist-frame-family).\n",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FGeneric%20specialist-frame%20family",
          "start_line":356
        },
        {
          "end_line":1015,
          "quote":"The family labels resolve inside\n`urn:stdo:bounded-context:reference-frame-evaluation`, owned by\nREFERENCE_FRAME, under the selected basis. Under bounded-context semantic\nresolution (PRODUCT_DEFINITION §5), `Product`, `Owner`, `Entity`,\n`Operator`, `Install` and the other labels do not become equal to\nsame-spelled Product, authority, domain or runtime concepts; every material\ncross-context seam needs an explicit relation (P1, P3).\n",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F11.%20Derived%20generic%20specialist%20frame%20set",
          "start_line":1009
        }
      ],
      "key":"generic_specialist_family",
      "label":"Generic specialist-frame family"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Testing frame, authoritative Product path and material combinatorial complexity are tier-2 terms owned and defined by ASSURANCE §7. This profile uses those definitions without additions.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":373,
          "quote":"Testing frame, authoritative Product path and material combinatorial\ncomplexity are tier-2 terms defined in ASSURANCE §7. This profile uses them\nas defined there and adds nothing to them (P1; rc.2 #testing-frame,\n#authoritative-product-path, #material-combinatorial-complexity).\n",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FTerms%20owned%20by%20ASSURANCE",
          "start_line":370
        }
      ],
      "key":"assurance_owned_terms",
      "label":"ASSURANCE-owned terms"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Executive labels the engagement frame that selects or confirms bounded activation configuration and consumes closed Worker and Reviewer results under existing project decision authority. It holds the complete Product view and current MVP or release mandate needed for priority, disposition and the next authorised action, without containing the complete workspace or becoming a universal semantic owner, controller, manager service or runtime observer.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":382,
          "quote":"Executive is this profile's label for the frame that selects or confirms\nthe bounded activation configuration and consumes closed Worker and\nReviewer results under existing project decision authority. It holds the\ncomplete Product view and the current MVP or release mandate needed to\nassign priority, apply disposition and select the next authorised action\n(P6, P2; rc.2 #executive).\n",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FExecutive",
          "start_line":377
        }
      ],
      "key":"executive",
      "label":"Executive"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Worker labels the constructor role of ACTIVATION §1 activated as a frame. It owns bounded construction and self-review within exact intake through operation authority inherited from the governing work relation. Writer specialises this role for documents and records.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":396,
          "quote":"Worker is this profile's label for the constructor role of ACTIVATION §1\nactivated as a frame. It owns construction and self-review inside its exact\nintake, through the operation authority inherited from the governing work\nrelation. It acquires no admission, publication, acceptance or continuation\nauthority (P6; rc.2 #worker).\n",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FWorker",
          "start_line":392
        },
        {
          "end_line":769,
          "quote":"It allocates construction to the Worker frame, specialised as Writer for\ndocuments and records; assessment, where it is required, to the Reviewer\nframe;",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F7.%20Non-hierarchical%20frame%20configuration%2FThe%20executive%20configuration",
          "start_line":767
        }
      ],
      "key":"worker",
      "label":"Worker / Writer"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Reviewer labels independently activated live-surface evaluation consumed by the assessment relation. It evaluates one exact subject and returns a closed result with evidence-bound technical triage when a finding exists, subject to externally owned independence, traceability, assurance-boundary and qualification-freeze rules.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":405,
          "quote":"Reviewer is this profile's label for the independent live-surface\nevaluation that the assessment relation of ACTIVATION §1 consumes, governed\nby EVALUATION §3 (independence and traceability) and EVALUATION §1 and §7\n(assurance boundary and qualification freeze), activated as a frame. It\nevaluates one exact subject and returns a closed result, with evidence-bound\ntechnical triage when a finding exists.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FReviewer",
          "start_line":400
        }
      ],
      "key":"reviewer",
      "label":"Reviewer"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Technical triage assesses one finding against its exact evaluated claim and basis. Severity grades the consequence if the finding manifests. Priority orders response relative to the complete Product outcome, likelihood, exposure, current MVP or release mandate, reversibility, dependencies, delay cost and available capacity. The Reviewer grades severity; the Executive assigns priority.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":434,
          "quote":"Severity grades the consequence if the finding manifests. Priority orders\nthe response relative to the complete Product outcome, likelihood and\nexposure, the current MVP or release mandate, reversibility, dependencies,\ncost of delay and available capacity. The Reviewer grades severity; the\nExecutive assigns priority (P6, P2).\n",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FTechnical%20triage%2C%20severity%2C%20priority%20and%20boundary%20effect",
          "start_line":430
        }
      ],
      "key":"technical_triage",
      "label":"Technical triage, severity and priority"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Current-boundary effect is the Executive's recorded determination that one finding blocks the current promotion boundary, requires narrowing it, or may remain an explicit residual. It is a decision projection, distinct from severity, priority, frame result and disposition, with no independent core-value mapping or decision power.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":456,
          "quote":"Current-boundary effect is the Executive's recorded determination of what\none finding does to the current promotion boundary: it blocks it, requires\nnarrowing it, or may remain an explicit residual. It is a decision\nprojection, a state this profile declares, not a result and not a\ndisposition (§8): it maps to no core value of its own and decides nothing\nby itself.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FTechnical%20triage%2C%20severity%2C%20priority%20and%20boundary%20effect",
          "start_line":451
        }
      ],
      "key":"current_boundary_effect",
      "label":"Current-boundary effect"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["A lawful Worker activation has occurred."],
      "definition": "A work result is the Worker's closed output to its declared consumer, the Executive in the coordinated branch. Its five construction-availability values refine the predicate 'a candidate is available', with total, exclusive mappings owned by ACTIVATION §3: candidate_ready→satisfied; refused→falsified; incomplete→falsified; re_entry_requested(authority)→out_of_frame; re_entry_requested(basis)→invalid_basis. These are carriers, not new dispositions, assessment or acceptance.",
      "exceptions": ["Activation refusal produces no Worker activation, evaluation or work result."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":490,
          "quote":"The work-result values are the five values of construction availability,\nthe refinement that\n[ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#construction-availability) defines for the\npredicate \"a candidate is available\". ACTIVATION §3 owns their grounds,\nmaps each to exactly one core value, and states that the mapping is total\nand exclusive after lawful activation. In this profile they are carriers,\nnot new semantic dispositions, and none of them is an assessment or an\nacceptance of the candidate (FOUNDATIONS §4 Results).",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FWork%20result",
          "start_line":483
        },
        {
          "end_line":512,
          "quote":"- `re_entry_requested(authority)` (`out_of_frame`): the Executive returns\n  the question to the decision owner the value names; and\n- `re_entry_requested(basis)` (`invalid_basis`): the Executive revalidates\n  the basis lock (§6 Drift locks) before any further activation.\n",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FWork%20result",
          "start_line":509
        }
      ],
      "key":"work_result",
      "label":"Work result and construction availability"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "An exact candidate is the subject identity required by transition evidence and assessment traceability. It is a checkpoint produced from the workspace, distinct from the mutable Source Project and from any later candidate created by repair.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":530,
          "quote":"An exact candidate is the subject identity that the transition evidence of\nACTIVATION §7 and the traceability of EVALUATION §3 require.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FExact%20candidate",
          "start_line":529
        }
      ],
      "key":"exact_candidate",
      "label":"Exact candidate"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The Product-owned Project Reference-Frame Basis projects existing authority's selection of outcome and work authority. It cites every material configuration source without becoming a new local-axiom authority.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":1130,
          "quote":"Goals, Product, requirements, accepted design, a ticket, release law or an\nadmitted bounded proxy selects the outcome and the work authority under its\nexisting owner. The Product-owned Project Reference-Frame Basis\n(PRODUCT_DEFINITION §7) projects that decision (P6; rc.2\n#1-existing-authority-selects-the-basis).\n",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F12.%20Complete%20engagement%20transition%2F1.%20Existing%20authority%20selects%20the%20basis",
          "start_line":1126
        }
      ],
      "key":"project_reference_frame_basis",
      "label":"Product-owned Project Reference-Frame Basis"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["The Product-owned basis adopts this profile."],
      "definition": "The baseline-adoption projection consumes the Product-owned basis and records the selected profile mapping, exact outcome, actor envelopes, evidence coordinates and revision conditions additional to the Product binding. It is neither a second frame-basis definition nor a source of projected authority.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":546,
          "quote":"A baseline-adoption projection consumes the Product-owned Project\nReference-Frame Basis of PRODUCT_DEFINITION §7. Where that basis adopts\nthis profile, the projection records the selected profile mapping, exact\noutcome, actor envelopes, evidence coordinates and revision conditions\nneeded in addition to the Product binding (§16). It is not a second\nframe-basis definition and mints none of the authority it projects (P6;\nrc.2 #baseline-adoption-projection).\n",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F5.%20Profile%20terms%2FBaseline-adoption%20projection",
          "start_line":540
        }
      ],
      "key":"baseline_adoption_projection",
      "label":"Baseline-adoption projection"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["The configuration is selected where construction of bounded changes and delivery across tasks need separate attention."],
      "definition": "The executive configuration allocates construction to Worker/Writer, required assessment to Reviewer, and coordination and bounded disposition to Executive. It is one lawful configuration selected for task fit, not the method default or a roster all work requires.",
      "exceptions": ["Where one sufficient frame covers the task, direct entry applies."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":775,
          "quote":"It is\none configuration, selected where it fits the task, not an inventory of\nroles that all work needs. Existing authority selects it or another\nconfiguration under §16, and a configuration with other frames, names or\ntopology is evaluated against its own task as ACTIVATION §1 Configuration\nstates, not by its distance from this one (P0, P2, P6).\n",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F7.%20Non-hierarchical%20frame%20configuration%2FThe%20executive%20configuration",
          "start_line":770
        }
      ],
      "key":"executive_configuration",
      "label":"Executive configuration"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The attention cycle maintains U, initially every known material evaluation not closed on the current basis, and chooses a finite dependency-ready activation subset M fitting assigned actors. It maintains a frontier and closed-result ledger rather than evaluators' undocumented working contexts.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":599,
          "quote":"U0 = every known material evaluation not closed on the current basis\n\nwhile U is non-empty:\n  select a finite dependency-ready subset M that fits the assigned actors\n  activate each member of M against the exact outcome and basis\n  keep assurance-independent evaluations free of unclosed peer results\n",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F6.%20Executive%20attention%2C%20evaluation%20and%20action%2FAttention%20cycle",
          "start_line":594
        }
      ],
      "key":"attention_cycle",
      "label":"Attention cycle"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The five drift locks concern unchanged outcome and mandate; exact current basis coordinates; distinct Product-chain roles; unchanged authority owners and grants; and complete material coverage plus declared result-return relations. They are checked before activation and disposition.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":667,
          "quote":"Before activation and before disposition, the Executive revalidates five\nlocks (P3, P6, P2; rc.2 #executive-drift-locks):\n",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F6.%20Executive%20attention%2C%20evaluation%20and%20action%2FDrift%20locks",
          "start_line":666
        }
      ],
      "key":"drift_locks",
      "label":"Drift locks"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A Product-chain basis records one Product or an explicit directed chain, preserving each mutable Source Project, current Product Definition, exact candidate checkpoint, Release Cut, Product, Install, Artifact, Development Product, dependent Product and composition-edge role as distinct. Each Development Product role binds one exact underlying Install.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":700,
          "quote":"A governed outcome may concern one Product or an explicit directed chain of\nProducts. Its basis records the distinct role of every mutable Source\nProject, current Product Definition, exact candidate checkpoint, Release\nCut, Product, Install, Artifact, Development Product, dependent Product and\ncomposition edge. Each Development Product role binds one exact underlying\nInstall identity.",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F6.%20Executive%20attention%2C%20evaluation%20and%20action%2FProduct-chain%20basis",
          "start_line":695
        }
      ],
      "key":"product_chain_basis",
      "label":"Product-chain basis"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Authority precedence decides which existing surface may select work, admit configurations, dispose results or require re-entry. Temporal and evidence flow carries activation packets and closed results. Frame topology records disjointness, overlap, conjunction, translation or composition; evaluation independence and Reviewer assurance independence remain separate activation relations. These structures may align where warranted but are never one hierarchy.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":737,
          "quote":"1. authority precedence, RF-009's structure of that name, decides which\n   existing surface may select work, admit a frame configuration, dispose\n   a result or require re-entry;\n2. temporal and evidence flow, RF-009's communication, carries activation\n   packets and closed results; and\n3. frame topology records disjointness, overlap, conjunction, translation\n   or composition among the evaluations actually used (REFERENCE_FRAME §7),\n   while evaluation independence and Reviewer assurance independence stay\n   separate activation relations.\n",
          "section_id":"repo://stdo-v3-generation/claude/9aee01ffa76cfbde1a6b8f1153a25bd6d71c216e/source/standards/EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#EXECUTIVE_BASELINE%2F7.%20Non-hierarchical%20frame%20configuration",
          "start_line":729
        }
      ],
      "key":"non_hierarchical_relations",
      "label":"Distinct configuration relation structures"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A steel thread is the smallest real runnable path from a supported Product entry through selected composition to a material outcome. This profile selects early establishment and bounded widening, or extension/revalidation of an existing affected thread, for early composition feedback at the cost of later widening.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line":879,
